the operator could still today use a weaker signature algorithm.  In the =
future, as crypto evolves, it is likely that some signature algorithm =
will become weak one day. If I understand correctly your text, you =
envision that the up-to-date client will remove the weak crypto while =
the server will continue to serve legacy clients with weak crypto. If =
that is the case, this seems to me an issue as the operator does not =
provides any guarantee the security level is equivalent to the one =
enforced by the CA.       =20
>=20
